error[ffi_field_type]: `Pt.x` is `int32_t` in `fixedbugs-2333-checks.h`, a signed 32-bit integer, not `i64` — clang read the header's struct and the field disagrees
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2333-a-group-header-s-macros-leave-the-probes-checks-standing.hero:12:9
     |
  12 |         x: i64  #~ ffi_field_type
     |         ^
  note: a group's `record` IS the header's struct (§4.19), so every field is at the header's own width and sign: correct `x`, or name the header that spells `Pt` this way
  fix (guess): declare `x` with `i32`

